    "agent_last_message": "The tool is built in `/workspace/output/` with the exact command you specified (`cmake -B build && cmake --build build`, run from `output/`). It compiles with no warnings under `-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic`, and it uses only the standard library.\n\nChecked against the spec: empty files, whitespace-only files, files with and without a trailing newline, runs of newlines, case folding, and punctuation kept on words. Exit codes 0 and 1 are confirmed for the cases I tried. A 300k-line, 7.7 MB file analyzes in about 0.03 s. I did not trigger exit code 2 because I have no way to induce an internal error safely.\n\nFiles:\n- `output/CMakeLists.txt`\n- `output/src/main.cpp`: argument parsing and exit codes\n- `output/src/analyzer.{hpp,cpp}`: streaming counting and top-10 selection\n- `output/src/json.{hpp,cpp}`: JSON output with escaping\n\nChoices I made where the spec was silent:\n- **Lowercasing is ASCII-only.** `\u00c9` stays as-is, so `\u00c9` and `\u00e9` are different words.\n- **Invalid UTF-8 in a word** is written as `\\ufffd` in the JSON so the output stays valid. Counting is still byte-based, so distinct invalid byte sequences can collapse into one displayed entry.\n- **Malformed input:** the spec doesn't define it, so I only reject missing, unopenable, or directory inputs, plus read errors. Files with NUL bytes are counted as plain bytes.\n- **Unwritable `--output`** exits with 1.\n- **Flags** accept both `--input path` and `--input=path`. A duplicate flag is an error. `--help` is treated as an unknown argument.\n- **Default build type** is Release when none is given, so the tool is optimized by default.",
